  "raw": ", which in part says:\n\nBeginning Jan 1, 2014, the definition of “premium day care” for purposes of section 3272 of this title includes a public preschool, provided by an individual or entity acceptable to the State Superintendent or authorized agencies, the rate of which: Comprises a segment that requires at least two times the average number of children per day aged four years and older who are enrolled in classroom-based child care programs offered under the international accounting standards put forth 42 U.S.C. § 6791(d)(3) each year.\n\nAs it pertains to public preschool programs submitted by certified early childhood centers (ECCs), there is no doubt that one of their main goals is increasing kindergarten reading achievement among their students; but I often hear complaints about the \"private playgroup\" atmosphere some of these centers have developed. My wife and I were almost persuaded to select our current favorite preschool because of its similarity in design to many other private",
